{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And the tablets.</b> Our predecessors said that they were created to be thus, as I explained at the beginning of the book of Genesis. In my opinion, the meaning of 'the work of Elohim' is that they were created thus in their proper form, and he mentioned this because Moses shattered the second ones." "Some say חרות is like חרוש, and some invert it: חתר (Ezekiel 8:8). The correct view is that it has no cognate; perhaps it is in the form of פתוח."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:39:45.420575604Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}